    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d109">

                <pb facs="0400" n="298" sameAs="frus:frus1943/pg298"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Hopkins Papers</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Prime Minister Churchill to the Presidents Special
                        Assistant</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hopkins</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, [<date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-05-21">May 21, 1943</date>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Hopkins</hi>. I should be glad if you could show
                    this to the President. <pb facs="0401" n="299" xml:id="pg299"/> I think the
                    Chinese ought to be told to lay off this aggressive policy while they themselves
                    are so dependent on the help of others.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d109-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W[<hi rendition="#small-caps">inston</hi>| S C[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">hurchill</hi>]</signed>
                    <lb/> 21.5.43</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d109-f1" n="1" xml:id="d109-f1-content">
                <p>Regarding Churchill’s concern over Chinese policy toward Tibet, see his remarks
                    during the meeting of the Pacific War Council, May 20, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg138">p. 138</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
